    "Tas divisible": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Divisible sandpile"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Un grain tombe sur une case tirée au hasard. Une case qui atteint le seuil bascule et en donne un à chacune de ses voisines ; ceux qui sortent par le bord sont perdus.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A grain falls on a cell drawn at random. A cell that reaches the threshold topples and gives one grain to each of its neighbors; grains that go over the edge are lost."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Une case qui porte %lld grains ou plus bascule : elle en perd 4 et en donne un à chacune de ses quatre voisines. Les cases stables gardent de 0 à %lld grains.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A cell holding %lld grains or more topples: it loses 4 and gives one to each of its four neighbors. Stable cells keep 0 to %lld grains."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Une masse est posée au centre. Chaque case qui dépasse 1 garde 1 et partage le reste également entre ses quatre voisines. Les cases pleines forment presque un disque.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A mass is placed at the center. Every cell above 1 keeps 1 and shares the rest equally among its four neighbors. The full cells form almost a disc."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Utilisé par le versement central, le tas divisible et la comparaison des quatre tas (de %@ à %@ grains).": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Used by the central pour, the divisible sandpile and the four-pile comparison (from %@ to %@ grains)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
